Beeline bundles FFmpeg to encode videos as WebM (VP9 video, Opus audio) before upload.

FFmpeg 7.1.2 (libavcodec, libavformat, libavfilter, libavutil, libswresample, libswscale)
  License: GNU Lesser General Public License, version 2.1 or later.
  Built without GPL and without nonfree components (--disable-gpl --disable-nonfree).
  Not built: libx264, libx265, or any other GPL library.
  Source: https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-7.1.2.tar.xz
  Text: tools/ffmpeg/licenses/FFmpeg-COPYING.LGPLv2.1

libvpx 1.15.0 (VP9 encoder, linked into libavcodec.so)
  License: BSD 3-clause, with the WebM patent grant.
  Source: https://github.com/webmproject/libvpx/archive/refs/tags/v1.15.0.tar.gz
  Text: tools/ffmpeg/licenses/libvpx-LICENSE and libvpx-PATENTS

Opus 1.5.2 (libopus, linked into libavcodec.so)
  License: BSD 3-clause.
  Source: https://downloads.xiph.org/releases/opus/opus-1.5.2.tar.gz
  Text: tools/ffmpeg/licenses/opus-COPYING

The FFmpeg libraries ship as separate shared libraries (libavcodec.so, libavformat.so, libavutil.so,
libavfilter.so, libswresample.so, libswscale.so) inside the app, unmodified from the pinned source.
You can rebuild them with tools/ffmpeg/build.sh and replace them in the application package.
build.sh holds the exact versions, source URLs, SHA-256 checksums, and configure flags.
